# mobileomarchy core package list (aarch64 / Arch Linux ARM + DanctNIX)
# Installed by install/packages.sh. Every entry here was verified to exist for
# aarch64 on archlinuxarm.org. Packages Omarchy installs that are x86_64-only
# are listed at the bottom of this file as comments, with the reason.

# --- Compositor and session -------------------------------------------------
sway
swaybg
swayidle
swaylock
wl-clipboard

# --- The shell -------------------------------------------------------------
# In 4.x the bar, launcher, notifications and OSD are ONE quickshell/QML shell
# (shipped as shell/ inside the Omarchy repo). waybar, mako, walker, elephant
# and swayosd are all gone -- do not reintroduce them, they would fight it.
quickshell
inotify-tools
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
polkit-gnome
wlsunset

# --- Terminals --------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are themed by upstream Omarchy templates (alacritty.toml.tpl, foot.ini.tpl).
# foot is markedly lighter on a Mali-400 / A53; alacritty keeps Omarchy fidelity.
alacritty
foot

# --- Capture ----------------------------------------------------------------
grim
slurp
satty

# --- Audio ------------------------------------------------------------------
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pamixer
playerctl
wiremix

# --- Touch input ------------------------------------------------------------
# Sway delivers wl_touch to clients and stops there: it has no on-screen
# keyboard, and `bindgesture` only ever sees libinput gesture events, which
# touchpads produce and touchscreens do not.
#
# squeekboard is the keyboard because it raises and retracts itself correctly.
# Sway advertises zwp_input_method_manager_v2 and zwp_text_input_manager_v3, so
# any OSK binding them is told when a text field takes focus -- and squeekboard
# keeps one layer surface for the life of the process.
#
# wvkbd was here first and does auto-raise (`--auto`), but it creates a fresh
# layer surface per activation and destroys only the newest on deactivate: 12
# created against 11 destroyed in one session, and the leaked one stays mapped,
# so the keyboard never goes away. squeekboard also ships a terminal layout with
# Tab/Ctrl/Alt/arrows, which wvkbd's generic layout lacks.
#
# Two gsettings gate it, both applied by install/config.sh: without them it
# starts, binds nothing and logs only "No system layout present".
squeekboard
# squeekboard's binary links libbsd.so.0, but the Arch Linux ARM package does
# not declare it (Depends On: cairo dconf feedbackd gdk-pixbuf2 glib2 glibc
# gnome-desktop gtk3 libgcc libxkbcommon pango wayland). So pacman never pulls
# it in and squeekboard dies at exec with "error while loading shared
# libraries". Listing it here is the fix until upstream corrects the package.
libbsd

# lisgd is no longer started (default/omarchy/plugins/mobileomarchy.gestures
# replaced it) but bin/mobileomarchy-gestures still needs it for anyone who
# wants the old edge-swipe bindings back.
lisgd

# --- Hardware ---------------------------------------------------------------
brightnessctl
networkmanager
bluez
bluez-utils

# --- CLI / TUI (the Omarchy idiom, and what is actually usable on this SoC) --
bat
bluetui
btop
# btop will not draw below 60 columns and a tiled terminal here is 47. bottom
# (btm) reflows, so it is the one that actually works beside the bar; htop and
# s-tui are the other two docs/apps.md names as installed.
bottom
htop
s-tui
dust
expac
eza
fastfetch
fd
fzf
git
gum
impala
jq
lazygit
less
man-db
neovim
plocate
ripgrep
starship
tldr
tmux
unzip
zoxide

# --- Telephony -------------------------------------------------------------
# Calls and SMS on the Quectel EG25-G. eg25-manager (modem power/GPIO) and the
# PinePhone ALSA UCM profile already come from the DanctNIX image; these are the
# layer above. gnome-calls and chatty are Phosh-era GTK apps, but they are plain
# Wayland clients and already laid out for a 360px-wide screen, which is exactly
# what this is. Together they cost ~115 MB resident.
#
# See install/telephony.sh -- their systemd units need replacing, not enabling.
#   gnome-calls  dialer and in-call UI
#   chatty       SMS/MMS
#   callaudiod   earpiece/speaker/headset routing during a call
#   mmsd-tng     MMS transport, used by chatty
modemmanager
gnome-calls
chatty
callaudiod
mmsd-tng

# --- Apps -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The set docs/apps.md documents as working, and the reason it is in the *base*
# list rather than the extras one: without it a fresh install has eight
# launchable entries, six of which are terminals, and pulling the drawer up
# gives you an app grid with nothing in it. A phone with no clock, no file
# manager and no browser is not finished.
#
# These were hand-installed for the docs/apps.md screenshots and never recorded
# in any list the installer reads, so the first unattended provision wiped them
# and the launcher came up empty.
#
# Both families are chosen for the 360px screen: GNOME's libadwaita and KDE's
# Kirigami apps reflow natively, and neither needs its own session -- they are
# ordinary Wayland clients under Sway.
gnome-clocks
gnome-text-editor
loupe
papers
foliate
portfolio-file-manager
kalk
kclock
kweather
keysmith
calindori
qmlkonsole
index-fm

# WebKit, ~260 MB, and the URL bar is at the bottom where a thumb is. Firefox
# and Chromium both run and both cost far more memory for no layout benefit.
epiphany

# --- Fonts ------------------------------------------------------------------
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd

# --- Support ----------------------------------------------------------------
gnome-keyring
libsecret
imagemagick
mesa-demos
mesa-utils
openssh
sudo

# ============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT installed
# ============================================================================
# hyprland, hyprlock, hypridle, hyprsunset, hyprpicker
#   -> These DO build for aarch64, but Hyprland hard-requires a GLES 3.0 context
#      (src/render/OpenGL.cpp: RASSERT on "either GLES3.2 or 3.0"). The Mali-400
#      MP2 in the Allwinner A64 is GLES 2.0 only. Replaced by sway/swaylock/
#      swayidle/wlsunset/grim+slurp.
#
# 1password-beta, 1password-cli, spotify, obsidian, typora, dotnet-runtime-9.0,
# aether, cliamp, asdcontrol, tzupdate, ufw-docker
#   -> x86_64-only (Omarchy's own repo has no aarch64 tree:
#      pkgs.omarchy.org/stable/aarch64/omarchy.db returns 404), and none are
#      sensible on a 720x1440 phone screen.
#
# tesseract / tesseract-data-eng
#   -> Not available for aarch64. OCR capture is dropped.
#
# walker, elephant
#   -> Not used in 4.x at all; the quickshell shell replaces them.
#
# yay, xdg-terminal-exec, ttf-ia-writer
#   -> Not in ALARM. Built from source; see install/build-src.sh and
#      docker/Dockerfile.builder.
